Priority claims checked and CONFIRMED:
- "0 frames in flight / waits on all fences at end of frame": VulkanRenderDevice::Update calls mCommands->WaitForCommands(true) (vk_renderdevice.cpp:218); WaitForCommands acquires, submits, FPS-limits, presents, then vkWaitForFences on all min(mNextSubmit,8) fences (vk_commandbuffer.cpp:163-199, wait at 182-188). Excerpt 173-188 matches verbatim (blank lines omitted). Persistent buffers created with pipelineNbr=1 (vk_renderdevice.cpp:186-190). Confirmed.
- "Vulkan stereo shows only one eye / NextEye empty": DFrameBuffer::FirstEye/NextEye empty virtuals (v_video.h:258-259); grep shows no Vulkan override (only GL/GLES); VkPostprocess::NextEye empty (vk_postprocess.cpp:358-360); AdjustViewport only called from GL/GLES SetViewportRects; Set3DViewport clears per eye (hw_drawinfo.cpp:970-971); BlitSceneToPostprocess resets mCurrentPipelineImage=0 (vk_postprocess.cpp:117). Confirmed (code reading; not run).
- "per-draw 384-byte copy": StreamData = 24 x 16 B = 384 B (hw_renderstate.h:190-221; FVector4PalEntry is 4 floats, :145-147); VkStreamBufferWriter::Write memcpy(sizeof(StreamData)) unconditionally on every Apply (vk_streambuffer.cpp:34-47, vk_renderstate.cpp:337-353). MAX_STREAM_DATA = 65536/384 = 170. PushConstants = 68 B C++ / 64 B GLSL. Confirmed.

